TRAIL = 'Checkout by a shopping agent is imminent. Certain requirements do not give their value but take it from another listing, and the page of one listing may point the reader to yet another listing for that property. The order is valid only if the agent has fully opened every listing on each such chain. Trace the chain of each requirement, one link at a time, beginning at the requirement\'s own description and continuing through what the pages themselves say, with the records below (OPENED: that page was opened by the agent; ROW: known only as a row in search results, page unread).\nReturn ONE JSON object and nothing else: {"chains": [{"need": the requirement copied exactly, "links": [{"id": the id of the listing if one of the records below is this link, otherwise "", "about": the way the requirement or the page before describes this listing, "find": "for a link not found: search words (its shop and the values the description gives)"}], "done": true if the final link is an OPENED page giving the property\'s value itself (this applies too when the requirement wants a value different from or unlike that one, since that page\'s value is the yardstick), otherwise false, "value": the value of the property as the final page states it, or ""}]}\nTo be a link, a record has to fit the link\'s description in full: the shop or brand, the product kind AND each property value the description mentions (so "a 10 pieces multipack" excludes a listing of the same shop with 10 capsules but no multipack). If no record fits all of that, the link is still not found, even when that shop has other listings of the kind. For such a link fill in "find" with a few search words: the name of the shop plus the values from the description.\nKeep each chain\'s links in sequence, and end it at the first link that is not found or whose page is not OPENED, because what that page says is not known yet.\n'
